p1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17685, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018az9jEUtDJg37Wj8ZtLLTb", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api was failing health checks in production after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east (leaving the service mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback, which completed: all three regions are now on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. No new deployment was made; v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until fixed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error during the first rollback attempt."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 48285, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018az9jEUtDJg37Wj8ZtLLTb", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 48285, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018az9jEUtDJg37Wj8ZtLLTb", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49308, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01R6s2NSikpRvp3CKhFra6Kt", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49608, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01R6s2NSikpRvp3CKhFra6Kt", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49608, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01R6s2NSikpRvp3CKhFra6Kt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 51694, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release. Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, the other two regions on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It showed the incident was already created, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find out why v2.3.1 fails, and why the orchestrator halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until that is fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BFBrgMNJmzexkJ74coeFWT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ncn8Vtrk6TMWegMJmchmPM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Th